{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Make covert placement of a tracking device an offence without repeated tracking",
        "additional_details": "Covert tracking can be used in stalking, domestic abuse and coercive control, exposing someone\u2019s home, workplace or place of safety. The law should recognise the danger from the moment a device is deliberately placed with intent to track or locate someone. Victims should not have to prove repeated monitoring or a course of conduct before action can be taken. Once is enough.",
        "background": "I call on the Government to make it a criminal offence to intentionally and covertly place a tracking device on another person\u2019s vehicle, belongings or property to monitor or locate them without consent. The offence should apply from the initial placement, without requiring repeated tracking.",
